A1. What is usually the price of freedom? ~ ALIMONY
A7. What kind of person takes life easily? ~ SUICIDE
A13. What kind of house would Jack build? ~ MANOR
A14. What do prohibitionists do to get full? ~ EAT
A15. What goes up but never comes down? ~ RATES
A16. What is half a printer's measure? ~ EN
A17. Who is the silent pardner in the marriage business? ~ PAPA
A19. What is it that makes most picnics "all wet"? ~ RAIN
A21. On what grounds does a Swiss yodeler procure a divorce? (Abbr.) ~ MT
A22. What was William Howard Taft? (Abbr.) ~ REP
A24. What do far-sighted people keep well stocked? ~ LARDERS
A26. What is often found around a girl's neck? ~ BOA
A27. What can you find water all around? (Abbr.) ~ ISLE
A29. What does prohibition make of many a man? ~ SNEAK
A30. What word describes the plight of henpecked husbands? ~ PENT
A31. What are the English always putting down? ~ ALE
A33. Name a tree that is found in Europe and America ~ ELM
A34. Who paints the outdoor girl? ~ SOL
A35. What is another word for "appropriated"? ~ ANNEXED
A38. What are bank employees never supposed to take home? ~ SAMPLES
A41. What is Judge Junior's staff-of-life? ~ GIN
A42. What is one way to down liquor? ~ SIP
A43. How does a girl advertise her engagement? ~ HERALDS
A46. How is the marriage knot tied? ~ SPLICED
A49. Name something always singular. ~ ONE
A50. Who was the third King of Judah who championed Jehovah against idolators? ~ ASA
A52. What is the cross-word puzzle fish? ~ EEL
A53. Where does the nickel go which gives you a ride in the N. Y. subway? ~ SLOT
A55. Where do good spirits come from? ~ STILL
A57. What count had no account before he speculated in oil? ~ SALM
A59. What tourist travels in a side-door Pullman. ~ BUM
A60. What word means "to be-characterized by great wickedness"? ~ HEINOUS
A62. What kind of lights are never bright? ~ DIM
A63. What is that indefinite article? ~ AN
A64. Name some useful culinary accessories. ~ POTS
A65. How do the drug-store sheiks look at the pretty Shebas? ~ OGLE
A67. What word means "to have existence"? ~ BE
A68. What is a prominent part of all necks? (Plural.) ~ NAPES
A70. What is found each week in JUDGE? (Adv.) ~ FUN
A71. What kind of sore is usually fatal? ~ ULCER
A73. What is rarely ever found hanging around the girls these days. ~ DRAPERY
A74. What did the knight of old like best about the Jews. ~ SHEKELS

D1. What dry country is all wet? ~ AMERICA
D2. What are the most popular parking places? ~ LANES
D3. Where is the big business man usually, when his secretary says he is "out"? ~ IN
D4. Name something often used in a clean-up. ~ MOP
D5. What kind of promise is easiest to break? ~ ORAL
D6. What did Romeo do for Juliet? ~ YEARNED
D7. What can always be found in their beds? ~ STREAMS
D8. What is the rainbow? ~ IRIS
D9. What is an ash receiver? ~ CAN
D10. What are movie stars supposed to have? ~ IT
D11. Name an evil spirit? ~ DEMON
D12. What are cultivated by the rich for show purposes? ~ ESTATES
D18. What is French for a step; a dance? ~ PAS
D20. Where did Noah spend the rainy season? ~ ARK
D23. What do schemers do? ~ PLAN
D25. In what river did G. W. go boat riding? (Abbr.) ~ DEL
D26. What proclaimed American liberty. ~ BELL
D28. What word means to have beauty or a pleasing effect? ~ ELEGANT
D30. From what flowers is opium obtained? ~ POPPIES
D32. What was Napoleon at the end of his career? ~ EXILE
D34. What did Old Scrooge rarely ever do? ~ SMILE
D36. What word means "born"? ~ NEE
D37. What is the finish of anything? ~ END
D39. What was poison to Cleopatra? ~ ASP
D40. What little word means "before" ~ ERE
D43. Who is the modern slave? ~ HUSBAND
D44. What would you give a fat lady who wanted to take reducing exercises? ~ ROOM
D45. What does a Chesterfield cigarette do? (Of course, you read the ads.) ~ SATISFY
D46. What well-known refreshment places are called by another name since a recent act of Congress. ~ SALOONS
D47. How would the reformers like our statues? ~ CLAD
D48. What should men wear over their eyes on windy days. ~ DIMMERS
D51. What complex is the Reverend John Roach Straton laboring under? ~ SIN
D54. Under what influence do even hard-boiled bachelors become sentimental? ~ LUNAR
D55. What does many an old hen do for her chicks? ~ SET
D56. Name something that has a lot of pull? ~ LUG
D58. What defamatory writing is punishable by law? ~ LIBEL
D60. What is it that comes higher on women than on men? ~ HOSE
D61. What word means to turn or swing around? ~ SLUE
D64. What are go-getters supposed to possess? ~ PEP
D66. What is one of the Best People On Earth? ~ ELK
D69. Who is not eligible to become the speaker of the house? ~ PA
D72. Who takes the survey? (Init.) ~ CE


